  "body": "Per https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#the-input-element:dom-lfe-labels\r\nevery `<input>` has a `.labels` property:\r\n```webidl\r\n[SameObject] readonly attribute NodeList labels;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe getter for this property is defined in\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#dom-lfe-labels as:\r\n> **Labelable elements** have a `NodeList` object associated with them that represents the list of `<label>` elements, in tree order, whose labeled control is the element in question.\r\n> The **`labels`** IDL attribute of **labelable elements**, on getting, must return that `NodeList` object.\r\n\r\nAnd [**labelable elements** is defined as](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#category-label):\r\n> `<button>`, `<input>` (**if the `type` attribute is not in the \"hidden\" state**), `<meter>`, `<output>`, `<progress>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`\r\n\r\nThus, AFAICT, the value of `.labels` is undefined for `<input type=\"hidden\">`.\r\n\r\nIn Safari 10 and Chrome, `.labels` returns null in this case, causing them to fail 1 test in\r\nhttp://w3c-test.org/html/semantics/forms/the-label-element/labelable-elements.html\r\nI haven't checked what other browsers do here.",
